            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: قيود, quyūd."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "على قيد (qayd) الحياة: alive, \"in the bond of life\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قيد (qayd) is built on the native Arabic root q-y-d (Lane), where qayd is the hobble put on a horse or camel, and qayyada, \"to tie; to note down\"."
            }
          ]
